"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, repo.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. BepInEx will then be downloaded into the REPO core files, along with the required mods, which will be placed in REPO\\BepInEx\\plugins. The game will then launch and automatically close after a few seconds to ensure BepInEx is correctly initialized.\nThen 'BepInEx.cfg' & 'REPOLib.cfg' (in REPO\\BepInEx\\config) will be modified to match the required setup.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"R.E.P.O. is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file (repo.apworld). When 'repo.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, a new 'Archipelago' button should appear at the bottom of your screen.\n\nEnter archipelago.gg in the 'ADDRESS' field, then enter the room’s 5-digit port number in 'PORT'. You can find this number on the website after creating a new room.\n\nThe 'PASSWORD' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nIn 'PLAYER SLOT', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nFinally, click 'CONNECT' and then, you can start a new run!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 3 revert options, using Full Clear will disable the other 2 until you turn it off.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for R.E.P.O. Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear BepInEx' option it will delete everything related to BepInEx and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.\n\nYou can also revert changes made to the configuration files by enabling the 'Patch Configs' option.",
